{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: write a design note, notes/2026-10-02-declared-acts.md, for declared acts, following assert 4e4134b4: a room's acts are declared by its application, and the fixed seven-act design is superseded. This is the top-priority Artroom work. The note covers:\n\n(1) What an act declaration contains: the act's name and body schema; who may perform it (roles, holder); what it requires of the room's state; what it holds exclusively, and for how long (leases); what it changes in the room's state; whether it lands files, and which checks and reviews apply; how refusals are worded in the act's own terms.\n(2) The primitives the room enforces, from which declarations are built, and the platform invariants that no declaration can change (plan decision 1: authorization and persistence invariants stay in platform code; plan section 9, \"Platform invariants that policy cannot change\").\n(3) Where declarations live and how they take effect: configuration under .artroom/**, admin approval, activation at an exact sequence number (as R-POL-9), and how a declaration is upgraded safely, including upgrading the evaluator itself.\n(4) Deterministic evaluation and replay: declarations use the pinned policy evaluator and per-act budgets (R-EVAL-1 to R-EVAL-4), so `artroom verify` on a fresh clone reproduces every decision.\n(5) What happens to a record whose kind is not declared, or no longer declared.\n(6) The seven current acts rewritten as the declared acts of the code-review application, showing that nothing they do today is lost.\n(7) The jam's acts as the second worked example (from notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md on request/jam-room-note): take a part, take the solo, pass the solo to a named player (a reserved handover the room enforces), signal, add a pattern, change key, change the house rules.\n(8) Impact and staging: changes to packages/contract, docs/protocol.md, the room, the policy runtime, the client, MCP and the UI; effect on lanes in flight; what this means for gate 1 (2026-10-05), with a recommendation for hugh to decide; a staged order of implementation requests.\n(9) Prior art with sources: gitseq's declared kinds (docs/concepts/record.md in ~/play/gitseq) and the dap project's goals for extensibility, so far as they bear on this design.\n\nPlain English per the repository's instructions. The note adopts nothing beyond assert 4e4134b4 and commissions no build.","body":{"conditions":"notes/2026-10-02-declared-acts.md is on main, approved by checker. It covers items 1 to 9 of this request, separates measured facts from targets, and lists every plan section, protocol rule and contract type it supersedes. Documentation only; implementation is requested separately after approval.","target_head":"df22d7713cc239f96a92f74596ee87509967a99f","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}